(text_box "Notes\n1. Function: two OPA1622, one per channel of the 3.5 mm output; each half its own\n   difference amplifier (R1 = R3 1.00 kΩ, R2 = R4 1.62 kΩ, gain 1.62, 100 pF across R2 and R4),\n   feedback at the half's pin, 1.0 Ω ballast to the leg (ADR 0012; BOM v1 lines 19, 37, 107, 108).\n2. Absent state: HPA_SE_EN pulled down on the host side: shutdown. A disabled output is not\n   high-impedance: never fitted but unpowered while the other stage plays (feature blocks #33-34).\n3. R4 returns to HPSE_REF_x, the same 3.5 mm sleeve sense as the DAC's REFA and REFB (PCB-A-16).\n4. Thermal pad (EP) to V- (PCB-A-08). Halves of a package symmetric, legs symmetric (PCB-A-09, -10).\n5. Links H20 #7, #8 on each rail branch, before the local capacitors (power tree §4.12).\n6. Unless noted: network resistors 0.1 % 0603 thin film, network capacitors C0G 50 V 0603;\n   ballast 1 % 0603; decoupling X7R 0402. Mute shunt footprints (BOM v1 line 100): open item." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 275.59 222.25 0) (size 129.54 26.67) (margins 1.905 1.905 1.905 1.905) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2277ccd5-0770-51e0-b66e-bd93ae26771d"))
(text "Interface" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 22.86 251.46 0) (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "88671727-17be-504f-8ca9-1ac25ce6381a"))
